    <details>
      <language>
        <terminology_id>
          <value>ISO_639-1</value>
        </terminology_id>
        <code_string>en</code_string>
      </language>
      <purpose>To record details of a medication preparation, including ,where necessary, details of mutliple ingredients, in the context of an infusion or ad-hoc (extemperaneous) preparation. The majority of dose-based prescriptions will have their precise preparation determined by available ward stock, or by pharmacy supply, while with product-based prescribing, the medication name carries details of the form and strength of the preparation.</purpose>
      <keywords>medication</keywords>
      <keywords>order</keywords>
      <keywords>prescribe</keywords>
      <keywords>therapy</keywords>
      <keywords>substance</keywords>
      <keywords>drug</keywords>
      <keywords>therapeutic</keywords>
      <keywords>otc</keywords>
      <keywords>therapeutic good</keywords>
      <keywords>ad-hoc</keywords>
      <keywords>extemperaneous</keywords>
      <use>For recording details of a medication preparation with in the context of the original medication order INSTRUCTION and carrying the prescriber's intent, or in the context of a medication ACTION where it serves of a record of the prepartion actually supplied.</use>
      <misuse>Use in pharmacy stock-control is out-of-scope of the design of this archetype.</misuse>
      <copyright>© openEHR Foundation</copyright>
    </details>
